WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.038
Marques:<i> Sega successfully
 positioned themselves</i>

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.340
<i> as the sophisticated
 alternative to Nintendo.</i>

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:09.442
<i> But 30 years later,</i>

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:10.710
<i> the question of which console</i>

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.545
<i> is better still persists.</i>

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:13.546
<i> So, today we're gonna do</i>

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:14.547
<i> our own tests</i>

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.049
<i> to determine a winner.</i>

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.317 align:start position:0%
This is Console Wars.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.387
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.588 align:start position:0%
All right,
so to jump right into it,

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:25.391 line:0%
we have our debaters
Dave and Joe

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.394 line:0%
<i> representing
 Sega and Super Nintendo.</i>

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:29.729
So these are the categories
we're testing today.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.364 align:start position:0%
Gaming and Graphics,

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:33.199 align:start position:0%
Sound Chip,

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start position:0%
and the Mascot.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.203 align:start position:0%
So, Dave, I'll start.
Gaming and Graphics.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.305
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:50% position:50%
This is Sonic 1.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.577
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.246 align:start size:66% position:34%
Blast processing is
how we're able to get

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:48.581 align:start size:72% position:28%
all these moving images

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:50.416 align:start size:56% position:44%
and tons of things
on the screen

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:88% position:13%
in quick succession
without things slowing down.

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:54.754 size:78% position:39%
So we'll see that if you,
like, lose all your coins

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.422
and they're all on the screen

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:57.790 align:start size:97% position:3%
- at the same time like that?
- Yeah, like that.

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:78% position:22%
Did you see that slowdown
right there?

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:00.760 align:start size:81% position:19%
Did you see that slowdown?

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:81% position:19%
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:88% position:13%
They can't handle all
of the sprites on screen.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
- And look at that 3-D ring.
- Oh, wow.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.534
Joe: That ring moving
at three frames a second.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.603 align:start size:59% position:41%
Three frames is
all you need, baby.

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.573 align:start position:0%
All right, so now it's time
to see the graphics
from Super Nintendo.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.676
If anybody is standing,
please sit.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.744
You're about to be blown away.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:21.814
So, I brought
Donkey Kong Country.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:25.485 align:start size:78% position:22%
Look at these
beautiful 3-D vistas that
we're seeing right here.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.753 size:78% position:61%
Yes, I don't need to go
a thousand miles an hour.

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:29.555 align:start size:69% position:31%
Look at these rendered
3-D characters.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:32.425 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look at that high-five.
Look at the frame rate of that.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.194 align:start size:66% position:34%
What a beautiful fall
that was.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.263
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start position:0%
So, I brought
some evidence on my iPad.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.303 align:start position:0%
I have some various sounds
associated with each
of these two consoles.

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.439
You can state your case
about which one is better
than the other.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.508 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( high-pitched chime )
- That's the sound

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.676
that whenever
Sonic picks up a ring,
you make that sound.

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.879 align:start size:63% position:38%
Now, if you go to,
like, a gas station,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.248
<i> you hear them
 open the register--
 it's that sound.</i>

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( high-pitched chime )
- That little chime
  gives me such joy.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:00.419 align:start size:72% position:28%
I'm glad your joy comes
from a gas station.

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:02.388
- ( ring )
- Fantastic.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Just a beautiful-- isn't it?
- Simple as that.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:78% position:22%
So that was when the game
first starts up,

00:02:06.425 --> 00:02:09.295
the Nintendo logo comes down.
You can hear the difference

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.697 align:start size:66% position:34%
between the tinniness
of the Sega Genesis

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.467 align:start size:56% position:44%
compared to
the robust flavors

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.701 align:start size:53% position:47%
you get from
a Super Nintendo.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:18.704 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( chime )
- ( high-pitched chime )

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:88% position:13% line:91%
- ( chime )
- ( high-pitched chime )

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:26.312 align:start size:69% position:31%
The sound chip
for the Super Nintendo
was designed by Sony.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:66% position:34%
The Genesis,
I think they just got
off the rack parts.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.317 align:start position:0%
Yeah, they just walked
into a drugstore

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.818 align:start size:91% position:9%
- and picked up
  what they could find...
- Pretty much.

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:34.754 align:start size:97% position:3%
- ...put it in their console.
- Pretty much.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.523
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:38.824 align:start position:0%
All right,
so let's start with Sonic.

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start position:0%
If you could take
a step forward.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.195
Sonic's cool.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.497 line:0%
He's fast.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.465 line:0%
He's got this cool spiky hair.

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:47.667 line:0%
I mean, check out
that spiky hair.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.235
I wish I had hair like that.

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.837
He's a freedom fighter.
He fights against--

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:69% position:31%
Dr. Robotnik
is testing on animals.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.475 align:start size:69% position:31%
Sonic says no to that.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sonic just looks like
your white friend with dreads.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.782 size:78% position:39%
Let's have Mario step up.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.518 align:start size:66% position:34%
Let's look at
a real American hero.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.220 line:0%
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.755 line:0%
Mario is a hard worker,
he's a plumber--

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.924 line:0%
one of the hardest,
most respectable jobs.

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:13.826
And he works with his brother,
so he's a family man.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:16.729 align:start position:0%
He's a drug addict.
He's always doing mushrooms.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
- That's not--
- He also takes prescription
pills. Dr. Mario.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:22.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
- He's not a doctor.
  He's saying he's a doctor.
- He's not taking the pills.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:69% position:31%
He gives you a lot
of medicine where they
counteract each other.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.540 align:start position:0%
Oh, yeah,
mixing prescriptions.
That's great.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.511
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:34.780 align:start position:0%
So, at the end of the day,
there's a lot to like
about both of these.

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:36.716 align:start position:0%
Clearly some pros
and cons to each.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.954 align:start size:59% position:41%
So, between
these two for me...

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.694
...just because I'm that guy,

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:50.429
I would actually probably lean

00:03:50.462 --> 00:03:52.398 align:start position:0%
towards me being
a Sega Genesis gamer.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.333 align:start position:0%
Mainly because I feel

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:55.635
like I would want
high-definition graphics,

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.637
and, of course,
it's matte black.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.673 align:start position:0%
So, my winner
is Sega Genesis.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.676
<i> ( music playing )</i>

